# 19. PCAP retrieval failure must NOT stop troubleshooting

Our Claude environment currently may block:

```text
api.ac5.mist.com
```

through an egress host allowlist.

We observed:

```text
DNS → success
TCP → success
TLS → success
HTTP → 403 host_not_allowed
```

Therefore:

```text
PCAP reference exists
```

is NOT equivalent to:

```text
PCAP downloaded
```

The engine must maintain explicit states:

```text
PCAP_REFERENCE_FOUND
PCAP_RETRIEVAL_ATTEMPTED
PCAP_RETRIEVAL_SUCCESS
PCAP_RETRIEVAL_BLOCKED
PCAP_VALIDATED
PCAP_PARSE_SUCCESS
PCAP_PARSE_FAILED
```

If retrieval is blocked:

```text
continue MCP investigation
```

and report:

> PCAP was available but could not be retrieved because of the execution environment.

Do not call this a Mist failure.

