# 27. Most important lessons from AP03 investigation

Use the following investigation history as design requirements.

We initially observed:

```text
AP03 full-EAP failures
```

and:

```text
AP03 FT success
```

This initially suggested:

```text
AP03 full-EAP path problem.
```

Then we discovered:

```text
same authentication failure signature
on multiple other APs.
```

Therefore the engine correctly had to reduce confidence in the AP03-only theory.

At the same time, controlled replacement testing showed:

```text
AP03 removed from original location
↓
AP07 installed
↓
client works

AP03 moved to another location
↓
same client tested
↓
initial connection succeeds
↓
forced reconnect
↓
connection failure
```

That is important AP-identity evidence.

Therefore the correct engine behavior is:

```text
Site-wide authentication failures
        +
AP03-specific differential evidence
        +
Controlled AP replacement evidence
        +
PCAP evidence where available
        ↓
Balanced RCA confidence
```

Not:

```text
One failure
↓
AP03 faulty
```

and not:

```text
Same failure elsewhere
↓
AP03 definitely healthy
```

